*.pem
*.pyc
__pycache__/
# Requests in flight between the web side and the camera side: someone is
# looking, re-find the phone, read this box. All three exist for seconds and
# live in /dev/shm on any machine that has it — see rpi/handoff.py. These are
# the fallback names, used where there is no RAM disk to write in, and still
# read on either machine so an upgrade cannot drop a request between the two
# sides restarting.
# Globs, because every one of these is written through a temporary and the
# temporary names are not all `.part`: the crop endpoint uses
# `.cropbox.json.<pid>.<n>.part` so two drags landing together cannot interleave
# into one file. Named exactly, three of those temporaries were missed, and a
# `git add -A` on the rig commits whatever was on disk at the time.
rpi/.viewing*
rpi/.recalibrate*
rpi/.cropbox.json*
rpi/live-frame.jpg*
# Advisory between this project's own scripts, so a second one says which pid
# holds the camera instead of dying with a traceback about a device. It contains
# that pid, and it is written into the checkout.
rpi/.camera.lock
rpi/config-preview.png
rpi/config.json
ssl/

# A shift's worth of offers: what was paid, how far, and when. That is the
# driver's own earnings history and, by the hour, where they were. It stays on
# the Pi, like the calibration and the live frame.
rpi/journal.jsonl
rpi/journal.jsonl.*
